NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1004,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,2,4,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":5,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0068,"rank":0.0948,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV000604","role":"target","render":{"description":"Urgent advice to take out fire insurance, because someone has seen the house on fire. Some time later the house burns down.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/42967","original":"[4.]\nMijn opa kwam ook eens bij buurman Scheper. \"Hest dien hoes in de brandkaaste Beernd?\"\n\"Nee,\" zei Beernd.\n'n Paor dagen later opa er weer heen.\n\"Beernd, hest 't hoes in de brandkaaste?\"\n\"Nee, nog nich.\"\n\"Dou hum d'r doadeluk in, want ik heb 't branden zain.\"\nEen paar maanden later, daor ging 't huis.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV005903","role":"helper","render":{"description":"When his farm burns down, a man says he saw the house on fire long beforehand but kept quiet about it.","place":"Wessingtange","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43264","original":"Veurloop.\nJoarn leden is hier brand west. Ik huilp de boer mit alles. De man stön aal man stil te kiekn en zee:“Nôn brand e ja.”\nIk vruig:“Hou komst door bie, wat betaikent dat?”\n“t Is wol al tien joar leden”, zee e dou, “op n oavend kwam k bie hoes en dou stôn alles in lichtelaaie. k Heb dr nooit over proot, mit ganaine, man nôn brand e ja.”","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.9175,7.14444]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV007406","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Lights are seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of fire.","place":"Musselkanaal","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44126","original":"Lichten zaggen ze vrouger voak. \"dr brandt weer wat\", zeden ze, zel wel weer gauw n huus aan goan. Dat geleuf was algemain.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.9325,7.01528]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV013008","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that all the white houses will burn down comes true; only the white church is still standing.","place":"Bourtange","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44092","original":"Oal vrouw K. zag vrouger ale widde huuzn in Boertange brannen.\n“Zai brant aal op”, zee ze. En t oal hef nog gliek kreegn ook. Allaind de widde kerke stait dr nog.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.01,7.19028]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Wessingtange.","Find Jipsingboertange on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[52.965,7.10139],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Jipsingboertange"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0987,"rank":0.2025,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ051006","role":"member","render":{"description":"A father warns his children never to walk in the middle of the road at night. After all, they might run into a funeral procession.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25083","original":"Heit woe noait lije, dat wy froeger by jountiid of by nacht midden op 'e wei roannen. Sels gong er ek altyd yn 'e berm lâns. Men koe ris tsjin in lykwein oprinne, wie syn sizzen altyd.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ112406","role":"member","render":{"description":"Because funeral processions need the space, it is best not to walk in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/30112","original":"Noait mat men by nacht midden op 'e wei rinne, fanwegen in lykstaesje, dy't altyd paed ha mat en dy't dan wolris tsjin jin oanstompe kin.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN009801","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Avoiding fireballs and fire-men; werewolf makes people carry him.","place":"Koningsbosch","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209005","original":"Vuurbollen en vuurman, weerwolf\nIn zijn jeugd tot zijn 25e jaar woonde verteller in een Duits grensplaatsje (zie boven). Daar werden omtrent vuurbollen en vuurmannen angstaanjagende verhalen verteld, evenals hier te Koningsbosch. Men moest vermijden in hun nabijheid te komen. De weerwolf sprong de mensen s avonds op de nek en liet zich dan een eindweegs dragen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ034606","role":"member","render":{"description":"You should never walk in the middle of the road, because you may be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22678","original":"Der woarde ús al hiel jong leard, noait midden op 'e wei to rinnen. Hwant it koe gebeure dat der in lykstaesje oankom en dan woarde men oan kant set.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Koningsbosch belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.0981,"rank":0.0837,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ022401","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Five weeks before a fire, a woman had already seen the house burn down.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20948","original":"Myn wiif Sjouk hat it hûs fan Ate en Ynsk hjir yn 'e Harkema sa'n fiif wike foar dat it echt opbrânde al yn 'e brân sjoen. \"Och Heare,\" sei se, \"Ate en Ynke har hûs brânt op!\"","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ057502","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A man came to his sick mother and saw a coffin in her house. But his mother was not dead and she lived another five years. Later the coffin really came.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0483","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25868","original":"Heit syn mem wie o sa min. Mem wie nei har ta gong. Heit kom even letter. Hy wie oan 'e doar ta, doe stie dêr de kiste al, mei 't kleed der oerhinne. It kleed waeide in bytsje op, doe't de doar iepenkom.\nDoe't er yn 'e keamer stapte, wìe beppe der noch. Sy hat noch wol fiif jier leefd. Mar hwat heit foarút sjoen hie kom dêrom letter wol krektsa út.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ058207","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A man saw lights somewhere, but in reality there was nothing. Five years later a tram came.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0492","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25990","original":"De tram is hjir kom yn 1911. Mar fiif jier earder seach myn swager de ljochten al. By Likele Pama - tichte by de Wilhelmina-hoeve - wie in wissel. Dêr seach hy de tram doe al rikjen. Hindrik de Jong hiet myn swager.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","5 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":5},"on_success":{"chime":5,"digit":{"value":5,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.7036,"rank":0.7241,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer has two sons. One cannot be got out of bed in the morning, the other has to do all the work. At some point he is","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12173","half":"top"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VODA_035_14","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The old farmhand is afraid. A young, fearless farmhand offers to take the horses to the meadow and bring them back from now on. One day the young farmhand also sees a burning candle on the gate and two floating ladies. The horses are restless. The farmhand knocks the candle off the gate and the two ladies vanish at once. The horses are calm again. From then on, however, the young farmhand is tormented night after night by the white lady, who wants her light back, and after six weeks he dies of it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"OIRSCHOT095","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The daughters tucked their skirts into trousers and wore a cloth around their hair. People saw white women around the castle and thought they were ghosts. But they were probably the lady of the castle and her daughters.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LAAN004a","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"On the border of Slochteren and Schildwolde they walked up and down an oak avenue in long white robes. They were never seen by day, but they were not afraid. They were in eerie places and in churchyards. They were also always at places where something had happened.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ001413","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He murdered his aunt for her money and since then it has been haunted there. All this happens close to the spot where the house of strong Hearke once stood.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"ZEEUW054","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"There were 3 chests, with a dog on one and on the 2nd a lion holding the key to the 3rd in its mouth, which the man has to take. He does not dare, and the woman takes leave for 100 years.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"LYST293","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Her dress is covered with feathers. Often in the morning some of these little feathers can be seen lying on the road. Her presence seems to have a fatal influence.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"LAAN005","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"There was one widde juvver (white lady) whose gown was too long, so everyone tripped over it. A ziever cut it off, and from then on things always went well for him and his family.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"ZEEUW049","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Since then Miss Jenne has not been seen again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"LYST030","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"In return she must run naked through the church. She does so reluctantly. Later a wit wief (white woman) can be seen on the land she was given. People are convinced that the woman's ghost still haunts it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"LYST265","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The mower flees. The mower's neighbour thinks the man probably saw a poacher or smuggler with a white sheet around him. It might also have been someone who wanted to frighten young girls.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"LYST041","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"They are badly frightened because they think it is the ill-omened figure of a wit wief (white lady). Later they see that the figure is not a wit wief but a white goat standing with its legs against the tree, eating the leaves.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0311. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c3"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c3"],"stack":["c1","c3"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2678,"rank":0.8234,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ063812","role":"member","render":{"description":"In Parken and in Rottefalle witte wijven (white women) haunt.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27145","original":"Hjir yn 'e Parken spoeken wite wiven en dat wie ek yn 'e Rottefalle it gefal.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEUNING003002","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Girls haunt at night the place where they were murdered.","place":"Broeksterwâld","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130952","original":"Ik arbeide op it sûkerijfebryk. Dêr fortsjinne ik twa goune yn de wike. Ik wier doe in jongfeint. Myn kameraten forgunden my dit ek noch. Op it Formanjepaed, hwer ik lâns moast nei it wurk, wierne troch in keardel twa famkes formoarde. Sont spûken dy dêr nachts altyd.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ057303","role":"member","render":{"description":"Several people have seen two witte wijven (white women) in the woods.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25852","original":"Witte wiven gingen altyd door 't bos van Jild Dyk. En so ferdwenen se weer. 't Waren twee witte frouljuu.\nDit gebeurde faak. Forskeidene hebben se sien.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ061710","role":"member","render":{"description":"On the heath in Drenthe witte wijven (white women) haunt.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/26899","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Broeksterwâld belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0371,"rank":0.4915,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ020208","role":"sill","render":{"description":"One evening people once saw two witte wijven (white women).","place":"Jistrum","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20586","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"ENGELB_02_006","role":"card","render":{"description":"Poplar wood glows in fine weather. A paper bag is mistaken for a ghost.","place":"Rossum","prov":"Ov.","year":1970,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128393"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ZEEUW045","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmer's son who works in the town in winter is always accompanied on the dike, when going home in the evening, by a white lady who floated above the ground and said not a word. Close to the farm she suddenly vanished.","place":"Terneuzen","prov":"Zl.","year":1923,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"J.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38971","original":"Witte Juffers\n\nEen boerenzoon van een hofstede bij Terneuzen kwam altijd 's winters in de stad werken. 's Avonds bij het naar huis gaan, moest hij een eind den zeedijk volgen, en als hij maar een voet op den dijk gezet had, verscheen er een witte juffrouw naast hem. Ze raakte met haar voeten den grond niet, en als hij iets zei, gaf ze geen antwoord. Soms sloeg hij er naar, maar dan was ze verdwenen, om op hetzelfde oogenblik weer naast hem te loopen; maar als hij bij de hoeve kwam, was ze er ineenen niet meer.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"OIRSCHOT002103","role":"card","render":{"description":"At midnight passers-by see a headless woman.","place":"Haaren","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"A.v.O.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/41651","original":"Vrouw zonder hoofd\nDa heb ik ok dikkuls heure vertelle deur m'n grotvaoder. \nDe boere ginge vruuger beer haole in den Bosch, en dan ginge ze deur de Essevoort. Dikkuls kwaome ze dan om 'n uur of twaolf terrug. En d'r kwaame ze 's naags 'n vrouw tege zonder hoofd. Nou, toen ze dà tegen iemand hadde verteld, zee die: nou da wil ik toch wel us zien. En ze ginge d'r ok um twaolf ure naor toe, en ze kwaame ze teuge. Hij ha zône schrik, toen ie ze werrekeluk zaag.","lang":"Brabant dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST278","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand makes a bet that he will bring the spit to the Witte Wieven (white women). One of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost). The Witte Wief could not run faster because she had trouble with one of her shoes.","place":"Ootmarsum","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"P.H.v.d.M.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13622","original":"Men vertelt dat ze woonden in De Hunenberg, een oud-saksische burg bij Ootmarsum.\nEen jonge boerenknecht had eens een weddenschap aangegaan, dat hij de Witte Wieve wel het braadspit durfde brengen. Hij reed te paard naar de burg en gooide het braadspit om de deur. \"Ik wol oe 't spit brenge.\" \"Zoa, dan zöl ie 't gebraod wên, mer eerst mo'k miene veters dicht hem.\" Ze was namelijk bezig haar schoenen vast te maken. De boerenknecht wachtte echter niet op haar komst, maar vloog weg, zo snel zijn jonge paard hem dit veroorloofde. Reeds spoedig hoorde hij achter zich de galop van een paard met 't witte wiefke erop. Hij spande zijn paard tot nog grotere snelheid aan. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ111314","role":"card","render":{"description":"You need not be afraid of witte juffers (white ladies) haunting about. The white ghost women can be driven away, the black ones cannot.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29719","original":"Men heart wolris fan wite juffers dy't spoekje. Dêr hoeft men net bang foar to wêzen. Wyt kin fordreaun wurde, mar swart net.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with J.","Jistrum. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c1","object":"window","text":"Jistrum"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1","word":"two","stained":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.679,"rank":0.375,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST274","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a wolf at night disappears when the farmer finds a wolfskin under his bed and burns it.","place":"Drogteropslagen","prov":"Dr.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"K.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13538","original":"Vroeger was hier een knecht, die 's nachts in een wolf veranderde en het de mensen dan lastig maakte. Onder zijn bed vond de boer op zekere dag een wolfshuid en verbrandde die. Sedert was de knecht verdwenen.\n(Verteld door een zeventig-jarige).","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL301","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand becomes a werewolf by means of a leather belt, which he hides. It is found and burnt in the oven; at once the suspected farmhand comes rushing up on horseback, but he is held back, and when the belt has burnt he says: \"I am freed!\"","place":"Echt","prov":"L.","year":1920,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"F.S.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35840","original":"De weerwolf \n\nOp de hoeve Bosscherhof woonde eertijds een knecht die een lederen riem bezat, welke de macht had, hem, indien hij hem omgordde, te betoveren als weerwolf. Geheimzinnig en zorgvuldig werd deze band telkenmale door de knecht verstopt en wat men ook deed, hoe men ook spiedde, men vond hem nooit. En geregeld hadden de mensen uit de omtrek, die laat huiswaarts keerden, de weerwolf te dragen. En ook iedereen herkende steeds de knecht. Men gaf elkander raad om wanneer men overvallen werd, de weerwolf op een of andere manier te prikken of te krab-ben tot hij bloed voelde of zag. Dan was men gered. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN002605","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a black cat at midnight by means of a rim is released after the rim is burned.","place":"Baexem","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208342","original":"Volgens tweede verteller was er op Nelishof te Tungelroy een knecht die elke nacht tussen twaalf en een uur afwezig was. Door een raampje ging hij naar buiten. Hij klom dan op de schansenhoop en kwam er als kat af. De boer had hem bespied en gemerkt dat boven op de schansenhoop een velg lag van een karwiel. Die had de boer daar niet neergelegd en hij zocht verband tussen de spokerij (zwarte kat) en dat karwiel.\nDit zou hij vernietigen als de knecht afwezig was. Op zekere dag had hij hem met schapen naar Antwerpen gestuurd. Toen hij een dag weg was stak de boer zijn bakoven aan en wierp de velg erin.\nOp hetzelfde moment verscheen de knecht en wilde de oven in. Het gelukte slechts met drie man om hem daarvan te weerhouden. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Limburg an animal was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1920.","That card names an animal. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"e67b9b37a212ac81","accepted_hashes":["1a8eedc7ee60253b758c446d4735d45247f64db974a4a405a07b7e4ee21ce7e6","86a0796ce1f322eb3683570ae50a8c676a14b7ef3400a0432c1a3ceafece056c","99bd3f99c90ce04edf2619fb103599dfc831a959ff4d72e7e181c823718c1db1","ae776beb236d57c1c3c39c7f24a02da674e6cac12c65546ac6d82a33ee79eb23","afb5fb8c1272f84124c74fbefa11d188938420a433a663fc59e218757ccb61f0"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0949,"rank":0.4963,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"member","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":null,"initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CBOEK477","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"On a wager, a farmhand must show that he dares to throw the spit into the Witte Wieven (white women) pit. He throws it and challenges the witte wief (white woman), who chases him. The farmhand jumps over the lower half of the door, horse and all. The witte wief throws the spit, which sticks in the middle post of the door.","place":"Bathmen","prov":"Ov.","year":1892,"code":null,"initials":"J.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/39631","original":"In de buurtschap Loo, op het erve Noever ging men een weddenschap aan met een knecht, dat hij het spit niet durfde gooien in de Witte-wieven-kuul; deze bevond zich daar ergens in de buurt. Hij sprong te paard en joeg derwaarts, aldaar smeet hij het spit in de kuil met de woorden:\n\nWit wieven wit\nHier breng ik oe een spit\n(of: Wat heb ie'j op oe spit?)\n\nDaarop had het wit wief gezegd:\n\nA'j zoo lang wacht\nDak mien eene schoe toeknuppe\nEn de aander toerukke\nDan zal ie'j 't gebraad wezen.\n\nDe knecht rende toen in vliegenden vaart huiswaarts, achtervolgd door het wit wief en voor de achterdeur gekomen, was de bovendeur los en de onderdeur dicht, maar het paard was nogal vlug en sprong over de onderdeur. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ENGELS000115","role":"member","render":{"description":"Werewolf leaps on people in the evening; as a helper with work; transformation into a werewolf by putting on a hidden coat, release after the coat is burned.","place":"Helden","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/57969","original":"Weerwolven:\nMannen, die wat laat op de baan waren, werden, vooral in donkere, stormachtige nachten soms besprongen door de weerwolf. Dit spookdier met gloeiende ogen sprong hen op de rug, en klemde zich met de voorpoten om hun nek. Ze bleven zich als een zware last aan de verschrikte man klemmen totdat hij ergens een huis bereikte. In de Broekbeemd, tussen Onder-Eijndt en Zandberg, stond ergens een holle eiken knot of poesjt. Er was een man, die als weerwolf bekend werd. Hij had een aparte jas; als hij deze aantrok werd hij weerwolf. Na zijn nachtelijke tochten verborg hij deze jas in die holle “poesjt”. Zijn buurlui ontdekten dit, en staken de “poesjt” met de jas in brand. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEMP298","role":"member","render":{"description":"A tenant farmer finds out that a young shepherd on his farm is probably a werewolf. He sends him away for a day, and he and his farmhands discover a wolfskin in a hollow willow. They set fire to it at home. The shepherd then comes back at a furious pace and tries to grab his skin back. When he fails, the shepherd flees to the hollow tree and is never seen again.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43423","original":"Het weerwolfsvel verbrand\n\nBij de pachter van de boerderij bij het kasteel Geusselt onder Amby diende eens een scheper, een klein manneke, dat de naam had een weerwolf te zijn. 's Nachts was hij nooit in bed te vinden, maar 's morgens lag hij er weer in. De knechts van de hoeve hadden dat al dikwijls bemerkt.\nWijl dit zo opvallend was, werd zijn doen en laten gedurig bespied en zo bemerkte men dan ook dat hij, wanneer hij 's avonds uit zijn bed kroop, naar een weide ging, waar heel eenzaam een grote holle wilg stond. Daar verdween hij iedere keer in.\nOm het fijne van de zaak te achterhalen stuurde de pachter hem op zekere namiddag naar een dorp, dat meer dan drie uur van de hoeve lag, om daar koeien te kopen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Bathmen belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0054,"rank":0.2821,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ044011","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. You must never quarrel with a werewolf, because then he will kill you. A girl always did sewing at other people's homes. Her suitor once asked her for a handkerchief. She gave it to him, and outside he tore the thing to shreds. After that he was normal again. He turned out to be a werewolf. Then the girl broke it off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24049","original":"Ien fan sawn soannen wie in wjerwolf. As in wjerwolf jin kriget, makket er jin dea, seinen se froeger tsjin ús. Men mat der noait rûzje mei krije, sei in muoike yn 'e Westerein, dan pakke se jo.\nMyn wiif hat in kammeraetske hawn, dy naeide altyd by oare minsken. Dy hie forkearing mei in feint.\nOp in kear wie er by har, doe frege er har om har bûsdoek. Hja hie him de bûsdoek jown, mar doe hied er dy bûsdoek yn alle moster forskuord bûtendoar.\nLetter wie er wer goed west, mar 't is wol útrekke tusken dy beiden. Hwant hy wie in wjerwolf.\nHja hat it sels oan myn wiif forteld. Dat kammeraetske wenne oan it Wyldpaed.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST189","role":"door","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELS001721","role":"card","render":{"description":"Man has to walk around with a werewolf for two days.","place":"Grashoek","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210547","original":"Weerwolven:\nIk heb eens horen vertellen van een man in Kessel, die twee dagen met een weerwolf op zijn rug moest lopen. Hij werd hem eindelijk kwijt, door hem tussen twee dicht bijeen staande bomen af te wringen. Hij had de klauwsporen op zijn borst staan.\n\nVerslag 50, Omzetting van de verhalen, verteld door Leonardus Kluijtmans, Helden, doorgegeven onder no. L291-17, op 26-12-1962. Van Nederl. versie in plaatselijk dialect. Helden, 4 nov. 1969\nIch heb èns huuëre vertèlle van enne mins in Kèèssel, dè twieë daag mèt te wèèrwolf hei motten drage. Hè woord öm kwiet, dor öm tössen twieë buim, die kort bei-ein sjtonge, van de rök te vringe. Later hei ’n de klauwsjpóre nag op zien boorst staon.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","3 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c3","object":"door","n":3},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P6","difficulty":3.3499,"rank":0.9535,"note":"Each story one number. In this order.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053702","role":"clip1","render":{"description":"Two men talking to each other find they have experienced the same thing: when they clung to a post during a boat trip at night, they touched a white figure. It is a ghostly apparition without a body. The figure then hurries along behind the hedge to the barn door.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25401","original":"Ik praette ris mei in keardel, dy sei: Dêr ha wy hwat bileefd! Wy wurken yn 'e polder. Mei de Feanster boat moest ik fuort by nacht. Ik moest troch hekken.\nIk wie by in hekke. Dêr wie in omstap neist. Ik krige de peal beet, doe taestte ik mei de hân op hwat.\n't Wie in gedaente yn 't wyt, dêr hie 'k op taest.\nFan kleare bare skrik haw ik der op houd mei de bôlleskeppe, dy't ik by my hie. Ik ha der gewoan trochhinne slein. Der siet gjin lichem oan. Doe bin 'k werom stapt.\nDe gedaente stapte achter de hage del en dy is ta de skûrdoar yn stapt.\nDoe't ik goed en wol op 'e boat wie, doe wie dêr ien op 'e boat, dy wie foar my itselde paed lâns kom.\nIk sil wol forbouwereard west ha en hwat wyt om 'e noas.\nDy oare sei tsjin my: \"Hwat sjochstû nuver. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ115905","role":"clip2","render":{"description":"At a certain place a gate keeps springing open: a ghost gate. Twelve men who take turns trying to push the gate shut at night see it spring open again every time. Someone was once murdered at that place. The ghost of the dead person still wanders about and keeps opening the gate.","place":"Eastermar","prov":"Fr.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/31213","original":"Op Bennema-state to Hurdegaryp stie de hekke altyd iepen. In kloftsje fan tolve man, dy kommen hjir út 'e omkriten wei, dy woenen dêr mear fan wite. Dy gongen dêr yn 'e nacht hinne en hâldden in weddenskip.\nIen foar ien dienen se de hekke ticht. Mar net sadra hie ien de hekke ticht dien of hy sprong direkt wer iepen. Deselde dy't it ús heit forteld hat wie ien fan 'e tolve. Hy wie de earste. As er de lêste west hie, sa fortelde er, dan hie er it net dwaen doarst. Sadra't er wer by de oare alve mannen stien hie wie de hekke samar út himsels tichtklapt.\nDêr moat ris ien formoarde woarn wêze. Dyselde fynt gjin rêst, en dwaelt dêr sûnt altyd om. Dan giet de hekke iepen, as er ticht is.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ081906","role":"clip3","render":{"description":"A peat skipper who is repeatedly startled by a naked little child behind his boat consults the minister. The minister asks the child, who died long ago, why it cannot find rest. It turns out the child drowned at that spot and was then buried without a shroud. The child asks the minister to request a burial shirt from the middle one of three women. The wish is granted and the minister hands the child the shroud with a wooden spoon. Now that its wish has been fulfilled, the child finds rest.","place":"Dokkum","prov":"Fr.","year":1970,"code":"SINSAG 0402","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32618","original":"In Ternaard woonde in turfskipper. Alle kearen as dat skip daar lei dan kwam der in naken kiendsje achter bij 't skip op. De skipper wist niet hoe hij daar mee aan moest. Toen is hij naar doomny gaan en het hem fraagd wat dat was.\nDe doomny kwam op it skip en dy het bidden en hy het it kiend fraagd hwerom it geen rust hat.\nToen het dat kiend seid, hy had gjin bjirhemdtsje.\nHy was daar ferdronken en nu kon hy daar niet rusten.\nIt kiend sei: \"Over it pypke sullen drie dames lopen.\"\nDe middelste moesten se fragen om in bjirhemdsje.\nToen het de skipper henengaan en die het die middelste dame daar om fraagd. En hy het it kregen. En doe het er dat op it turfplak neergooid.\nEn doe het de doomny dat himdtsje dat kiend toereikt met een houten sleef. …","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ058602","role":"inside","render":{"description":"The Jankemeer and the Trientsjemeer lie close to each other. A certain Janke drowned herself in the Jankemeer because her boyfriend had broken off their courtship. A certain Trientsje drowned in the Trientsjemeer. People heard noises then. A man with a white back in a waistcoat still haunts the place.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"TM 2601","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/26058","original":"By de Skieding hienen jo twa dobben. Oan 'e iene kant fan 'e wei wie de Janke-dobbe, oan 'e oare kant de Tryntsje-dobbe.\nDer wie in sekere Janke, dy hie in feint. Dy feint hie de forkearing mei har út makke, en doe hat Janke har dêr forsûpt. Sa hat dy dobbe de namme fan Janke-dobbe krigen. Sûnt hja har dêr forsûpt hat, spoeket it dêr.\nYn 'e oare dobbe ha se in sekere Tryntsje forsûpt. Tryntsje hat doe lûd jown. Letter hearden se dêr altyd lûden. In man mei in wite rêch yn 't festje spoeket dêr noch altyd om.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","note":"This one I keep apart."},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Each story counts.","The first number is 2.","2 — 12 — 3."],"lock":{"kind":"number3","salt":"e67b9b37a212ac81","accepted_hashes":["91fa562e086603aac094429ed83c1dbb6d55024a160f04ac6756c2500a54584f"]},"on_success":{"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.5242,"rank":1.2875,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ036919","role":"member","render":{"description":"A dead woman was buried in a shroud that was too long and keeps haunting after her death, calling 'Too long! Too long!'. After the minister has learned her problem from her, a piece of the shroud is torn off. Her ghost has never shown itself again.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22968","original":"Yn 'e Smoarhoeke yn 'e Harkema wie in frou stoarn. Dy hie in bierkleed omkrige yn 'e kiste, dat hie to lang west.\nDoe koe dat minske de rêst net fine. En doe kom se elke joun by de famylje en dan rôp se: \"To lang! To lang!\"\nDoe ha dy lju doomny ophelle en dy hat har oansprutsen. Doe sei se, har bierkleed wie to lang, dêr moest in stik ôf.\nDoe is dêr in stik ôfskuord woarn en sûnt hat se har net wer fortoand.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ014310","role":"member","render":{"description":"A widower's second wife wore the first wife's clothes. But the children sometimes saw their first mother haunting in the wardrobe. The father did not believe it, but in the end sent for the minister. The spirit wanted clothes for her children to be made from her clothing, not for them to be worn by another woman.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19663","original":"Der leefde in man, dy forlear syn wiif. Hja hie in hiele protte klean fan har sels yn 'e kast. De man troude wer en sei tsjin it twadde wiif: \"Jo kinne dy klean wol drage.\"\nDoe seagen de bern har mem hyltyd wer kommen. Hja spoeke en roan nei de kast ta. Dat gebeurde wit hoe faek. Allinne de bern seagen it en sy fortelden it oan har heit. Mar dy woe 't net leauwe.\n\"Praetsjes\", sei er. Mar de bern bleauwen der by dat har mem nou en dan kom. Dat doe moest er 't op 't lêst ek wol leauwe. Doe helle hy de dûmny der by. Dy spruts it spoek oan.\n\"Hwat is jou bigearte?\" frege er.\n\"Dat de bern klean krije út de klean fan my\", sei se.\n\"Oaren matte se net oan ha.\"\nDat woarde dien en doe kom se net werom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ109806","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A man plays at being a minister and mocks everything in his sermon. He never does it again, because at night the devil came to his bed.","place":"Feanwâlden","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38551","original":"Achter it café yn Feanwâlden stienen froeger banken. Dêr hâldde in kammeraet fan my in preek. Hy wie sabeare doomny. Hy spotte dat it hwat die en hie oeral de gek mei.\nDoe't er dy nachts op bêd lei, kaem de duvel by him. Doe die er it lekken oer de holle hinne, sa binaud waerd er.\nNoait hat er sokke dingen letter wer úthelle.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ013022","role":"member","render":{"description":"It sometimes happened that the dead came back when people did not keep the promises they had made during the dead person's life. The minister then had to come to ask the dead person what he wished.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19482","original":"It gebeurde wol, fortelde beppe, dat lju dy't stoarn wienen, weromkommen, as de minsken har net hâldden oan 'e bilofte dy't se sokken by har leven dien hienen. Dan moest der in dûmny by komme om sa'n forstoarne to freegjen hwat er winske.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Feanwâlden belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.2143,"rank":0.7917,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer lives in a haunted farmhouse. When an old soldier comes begging, the farmer asks whether he will keep watch.","place":"Uitdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1903,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35028","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEMP173","role":"half","render":{"description":"Fortunately he knows that you must be bold with ghosts and never give them their way. He follows the ghost but refuses to carry out the tasks it gives him. The next day the craftsman has grey hair, but he is in possession of a treasure. From then on he can live off his wealth.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ015407","role":"half","render":{"description":"When she later goes to feed the pigs, the child's ghost keeps appearing. The child keeps putting its little hands on the pig trough.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ073804","role":"half","render":{"description":"Then Ruerd threatened to knock him down if he did not wait. The other then stopped. When Ruerd reached him, the other grabbed him several times and threw him over the trees. The next day they found him unconscious with all his ribs broken.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"At midnight the soldier sees six ghosts pass by; high-ranking officers who dig a hole by the haystack with their sabres. The ghosts pull up a kettle of gold coins and hide it again. In the morning the soldier asks the farmhand to help him dig. By the haystack they find the kettle of gold and take it. At night the ghosts come to dig again, but find nothing and never return. The farmer is pleased and offers the soldier lodging and a reward. The soldier accepts the lodging, but by now he has enough money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"six"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ093904","role":"half","render":{"description":"He died in an accident with a horse and now his treasure lies there under the ground. The old man haunts the place and people are terrified. The old man keeps coming closer.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ082909","role":"half","render":{"description":"The man cannot bear it and fetches the minister. The minister says to the ghost: 'If you are of God, come to me; if you are of the devil, depart.' The ghost disappears and never comes back.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘farmer’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c5","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c5"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1","word":"six","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
